nse of comfort  throughout a lot of the girls you know  with claudia and then with sophie and  christy at the end um talking about her  dad and then talking about mimi so  they're just those things that i'm  excited to have marianne be that kind of  nurturing soul in that comfort side that  we didn't get to see throughout the  first season because she was usually the  one that's crying she says sorry all the  time um so i'm just excited for you guys  to see that part oh dawn you look super  tan three weeks in southern california  where the sunshine is advertised  i feel like a whole new person kendra  which spoiler meant the most to you in  season two what are you most excited for  fans to see well in season one dawn was  all good with everything she you know  had her life put together and she never  got upset and then in season two you  really see her bottle up all of her  emotions until she kind of just explodes  and i think it's really you see how she  handles um having anxiety all the girls  struggle through something and this is  specifically what dawn struggles with  and i think it's really important to see  that for other people who might be  struggling with anxiety to see that like  you know they're not alone and there's  other people that have it and struggle  with it  and you just really get to see her  handle that that was like clockwork  smoothest silk a well-oiled machine  you guys are awesome if we do get a  third season what is something that you  would love to see for your character  next to the end what would you like to  see from mallory if we get another  chapter i would definitely like to see  more of her family more of her family  life i think we got to see a little bit  this season but that's one of my hopes  for season three and we're keeping our  fingers crossed i loved filming all the  ballet scenes so much this season you  saw jessie and how she was a background  character in her school performance and  how she's trying to accept that that 